--- body ---
## Context
Recurring complaint (author, 2026-10-20): merged PRs carry no record of which model ran at which effort level for which step (plan, execute, each review seat, gate, roar). Evidence of the pattern: review attribution for PR 1466 lives only in the unmerged PR 1481; several main commits carry no Co-Authored-By trailer; `memory/evidence/review-attribution-pr14xx-pending.md` files accumulate as stopgaps. Unknown yet: where the loss happens (the runtime does not state effort, the route record is never written, or it is written outside the PR).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Inventory of where model, effort and step identity is available per step (runtime, route cache, verdict artifacts, commit trailers) and where it is lost; unstated effort is recorded as "not stated", never guessed
- [ ] One mandatory attribution record per merged PR, at a fixed place that lands with the PR (PR body block or file in the branch), listing step, model, effort, route and independence basis
- [ ] `/merge` (or its gate) refuses or warns when the record is absent; positive control: a PR without it is flagged
- [ ] Backfill decision for the pending attribution files (e.g. PR 1481) stated: land, fold into the new mechanism, or drop

## Children
- 1148 inventory of where identity is lost (exit 1)
- 1149 PR-body attribution block and /merge warning (exits 2-3), blocked by 1148
- 1150 fold pending attribution files (exit 4), blocked by 1149

Decisions 2026-10-20: warn at /merge, record in the PR body, fold the pending files. Transcript recovery stays out (ticket 1142 and the 1145-era steers). This ticket closes after the integration review.
